# RFC-0013: Admin Editors

Status: Active

## Abstract

Create and edit of admin entities happen on their own routes. Deleting an entity
happens in its editor's DangerZone, never from a list. A media insert picker may
be a dialog. An entity editor MUST NOT.

## 1. Routes

- Create MUST be `/new` under the list (or `/new/$type` when the create form is
  typed, as with authentication schemes).
- Edit MUST be `/$id` under the list (or a nested `/$id` the list already owns,
  such as `/menus/$id/items/$itemId`).
- Entity URLs MUST NOT carry list query params (RFC-0010).

## 2. Dialogs

- Editor dialogs are FORBIDDEN. Create and edit open a page.
- Confirm dialogs are ALLOWED (delete, discard draft, unpublish).
- Insert pickers (media / FileUpload) MAY be dialogs. They insert a URL into an
  already-open editor; they do not edit an entity.

## 3. Lists

- Row actions are one overflow menu (`RowActions`) and hold only
  non-destructive actions. A list MUST NOT delete, clear, or revoke, except
  trash (§5).
- The name/title column is the edit link when an edit route exists.
- Back links from create, edit, and detail MUST use `ListBackLink` and restore
  the remembered list search for that `listKey`.

## 4. Remembered list query

- When a list renders, it MUST store the applied query in `sessionStorage` under
  `raytha.list:${listKey}` so `ListBackLink` can restore it.
- Sidebar and command-palette links to the bare list path remain a reset.

## 5. Danger Zone

- Every destructive action on an entity (delete, permanent delete, revoke,
  reset) lives in a `DangerZone` at the bottom of that entity's edit page, with
  a confirm dialog that names what breaks.
- An entity with no edit page gets a detail page (`/$id`) to hold its
  DangerZone, as media items do at `/media/$id`.
- Bulk maintenance (clearing logs, finished background tasks) is not an entity
  delete. It lives on the Maintenance page behind a confirm dialog.
- Trash is the one list exception. A trashed item has no editor, so each trash
  row offers Restore and Delete permanently, and permanent delete is confirmed.
- `CrudListPage` has no delete prop, and `RowActions` has no destructive
  variant, so a row-menu delete cannot be written.
